			"Message": "fix(Cocoon): Restore 17 closing parentheses stripped by prior bulk refactor\n\nThe `) → ;` bulk statement-termination refactor from the Effect-TS removal erroneously stripped the closing `)` from every call expression in Source/Bootstrap/Implementation/Cocoon/Main.ts, leaving 17 malformed statements across the PostHog telemetry bridge, the setImmediate lifecycle hook, the parent-death watchdog, and bootstrap error handling.\n\nRestore `)` before `;` in every affected expression: PostHogBridge.Initialize, Date.now, CaptureEntryLoad, CaptureEntryLoaded, the setImmediate arrow closing, process.stderr.write (6 call sites), process.exit (2 call sites), setInterval, ParentWatch.unref, runBootstrap, StartWebSocketServer.catch, and the main() entry call.\n\nAll expressions now compile with balanced parentheses and valid statement syntax.",
			"SHA": "763b8eceddf4e5c9a854957de223742f987cd9d3"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-13T02:32:37Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				564,
				1
			],
			"Message": "fix(Cocoon): Restore missing closing parenthesis in dynamic import\n\nThe prior `)` → `;` bulk refactor stripped the closing parenthesis from the dynamic `import()` expression in the PostHog telemetry bridge, leaving a malformed `import(...;` call.\n\nAdd the missing `)` before `;` to restore valid syntax for the ConditionalImport pattern. This is a pure syntax fix with no behavioral change.",
			"SHA": "bbb622b182c480e02a3dd3371c821a6dbc7253d8"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-13T02:32:00Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				564,
				6
			],
			"Message": "fix(Cocoon): Restore missing closing parentheses in semicolon-terminated calls\n\nSix `)` → `;` replacements applied during the prior bulk refactor inadvertently removed the closing parenthesis from call expressions that still needed them, leaving malformed syntax in Logger, Telemetry, and four VscodeAPI Wrap namespaces.\n\nRestore the `)` before `;` in each case: Logger.Debug spread argument, Telemetry metric/span Map constructors and event-mutation calls, and all four WrapNamespaceWithHeuristics invocations. Every affected expression now correctly terminates as a complete statement with balanced parentheses.\n\nThis is a pure syntax fix with no behavioral or semantic changes.",
			"SHA": "fe6b15d5675a4df8fc3be371461d0dbdf0ee92f9"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-13T02:31:36Z",
			"File": [
				"⡇⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				564,
				58
			],
			"Message": "docs(Cocoon): Update Test namespace header to reflect fully wired lifecycle\n\nThe module-level JSDoc in `Tests/Namespace.ts` still described the Test API shim as a stub awaiting Mountain/Sky wiring. Update the header block to state that `SendToMountain` + `Output/Source/Service/CEL/Expose/Accessor.ts` now complete the Cocoon → Mountain → Sky lifecycle for `TestRun.*` events and Testing panel rendering.\n\nAlso add a separating blank line before the `Context.SendToMountain(\"tests.run_started\", ...)` call for readability, consistent with the adjacent `SendToMountain` pattern.",
			"SHA": "493610c729c114b6def388afa07e15d3df06beb7"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-12T23:40:21Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				564,
				1
			],
			"Message": "feat(Cocoon): Bridge test controller lifecycle and run results to Mountain\n\nForward test controller registration, run start, individual results, and run completion events from the VS Code Test API shim to Mountain via `SendToMountain` notifications. This enables the Sky UI to track test execution state in real time through the gRPC bridge.\n\n- `CreateTestController`: emit `tests.controller_created` on registration\n- `SetState`: emit `tests.run_started` on first result, `tests.result` per item\n- `Run.End`: emit `tests.run_ended` with aggregated results and output buffer\n\nFollows the `)` → `;` statement-termination convention established in the prior bulk refactor.",
			"SHA": "d6badc840bdc981438cfa11f958388e07fa4d09b"
		}
	],
